CommitDate: Tue Sep 29 18:34:20 2026 -0500

    fix(health): resolve default namespace in keys probe — fresh install no longer degraded
    
    probeKeysStore() passed no namespace into the keys query, so on a fresh
    install (empty namespaces root, default namespace never created) /health
    answered 503 forever with keys_error "Namespace 'undefined' does not
    exist".
    
    The probe now resolves the config default namespace (the same
    resolution every other keys consumer uses via resolveNamespaceName) and
    passes that resolved name on; runKeysQuery names the resolved namespace
    in its error string instead of the raw argument. A not-yet-existing or
    empty namespace directory reports healthy (fresh install — no keys
    exist, nothing to fail on); genuine store errors (corrupt JSONL, corrupt
    manifest, connection loss) still degrade /health.
    
    Tests: probeKeysStore treats a missing namespace as healthy, resolves
    the default through DUCKBRAIN_NAMESPACE, still returns a short error on
    a corrupt manifest; createHealthHandler over an empty namespaces root
    returns 200 healthy with keys_error null (HEALTH-KEYS-UNDEFINED-001).
    
    Addresses HEALTH-KEYS-UNDEFINED-001.
    
    Co-authored-by: Hermes Foreman <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
